{"vid":"BYtYm-xyKR8","source":"BYtYm-xyKR8.en.json3","lang":"en","cues":[{"t":2.4,"txt":"Budgeting was, I felt like one of my"},{"t":5,"txt":"greatest superpowers."},{"t":7,"txt":"And the word budget to a lot of people instills,"},{"t":10.2,"txt":"like this kind of fear that you have to live in"},{"t":12.3,"txt":"deprivation. But what my budget did for me was give"},{"t":16.6,"txt":"me the opportunity to spend money on the things that"},{"t":19.7,"txt":"were super important to me."},{"t":21.4,"txt":"My name is Naseema McElroy."},{"t":23.2,"txt":"I'm 44 years old."},{"t":25,"txt":"I work as a labor and delivery nurse in the San"},{"t":28.2,"txt":"Francisco Bay area."},{"t":39.4,"txt":"That second job ironically covers a lot of my child"},{"t":42.8,"txt":"care expenses as a single mom."},{"t":45.2,"txt":"I actually took three months off of work just to focus on"},{"t":49.7,"txt":"my family and recovering, and finding a little bit of"},{"t":53.9,"txt":"that balance."},{"t":60.1,"txt":"I invested about $50,000 into my business,"},{"t":63.6,"txt":"into building out some things in the back end."},{"t":66.9,"txt":"My business operates at a loss at the current moment"},{"t":70.6,"txt":"because there are some really exciting things"},{"t":73.6,"txt":"coming up."},{"t":79.5,"txt":"I am a mom of three beautiful girls."},{"t":83.2,"txt":"Having childcare is rather a big line item in my"},{"t":87.6,"txt":"budget. I prioritize financial independence,"},{"t":92.2,"txt":"so as soon as I got to the point where I was able to"},{"t":96.8,"txt":"max out a 403(b) and a 457 and invest in a Roth"},{"t":101.5,"txt":"IRA, I started investment accounts for my kids."},{"t":115.9,"txt":"The Bay area is very expensive,"},{"t":118.5,"txt":"and I really feel like when it comes to living"},{"t":121.1,"txt":"comfortable, you have to be a little bit creative."},{"t":126,"txt":"Always try to keep my mortgage under 30% of my"},{"t":129.4,"txt":"income. So I do live a little bit further east in"},{"t":132.3,"txt":"the Bay Area. I always have a room in my house where I"},{"t":135.7,"txt":"let my coworkers or travel nurses stay,"},{"t":138.5,"txt":"and that further decreases my housing costs."},{"t":141.3,"txt":"I don't think that debt is a bad thing."},{"t":143.8,"txt":"I think that we have to be intentional about the"},{"t":146.5,"txt":"choices we make and the decisions that we make"},{"t":149.5,"txt":"around debt. All my debts have been intentional."},{"t":151.8,"txt":"So the debt for my mortgage."},{"t":153.9,"txt":"Of course, it would be very hard to buy $1 million house"},{"t":157.9,"txt":"cash. The other debt is primarily to grow my"},{"t":161.2,"txt":"business and invest back into my business."},{"t":164.2,"txt":"I am definitely a credit card girly."},{"t":166.4,"txt":"I do have about 20 credit cards."},{"t":168.8,"txt":"I was heavy in the try to be a credit card like hacker,"},{"t":173.5,"txt":"and now it's just because I like having access to extra"},{"t":178.1,"txt":"resources."},{"t":183.9,"txt":"I grew up kind of poor. I was raised by a single dad"},{"t":186.7,"txt":"in West Oakland, but I went to a very"},{"t":190.2,"txt":"affluent school and one of the most richest"},{"t":192.7,"txt":"neighborhoods in Oakland."},{"t":194.2,"txt":"So I was surrounded by people that didn't look like"},{"t":197.4,"txt":"me, that had wealth."},{"t":198.9,"txt":"And so I assumed that wealth wasn't for me because we"},{"t":201.5,"txt":"definitely didn't have it."},{"t":217,"txt":"My biggest money mistakes in my 20s was investing in real"},{"t":221.1,"txt":"estate and not really understanding what the"},{"t":223.8,"txt":"investment meant, not really understanding the"},{"t":226.5,"txt":"cost of home ownership and the cost of being a landlord"},{"t":231.3,"txt":"and dealing with a lot of personalities."},{"t":234.2,"txt":"And those lessons caused me to have two short sales and"},{"t":237.9,"txt":"two foreclosures, and ultimately have to file"},{"t":240.6,"txt":"for bankruptcy in my 20s in 2015."},{"t":243.4,"txt":"I had just bought this brand new house and I had 36"},{"t":246.2,"txt":"windows, and they all needed blinds on them."},{"t":248.5,"txt":"And so I had to borrow money from my sister."},{"t":250.9,"txt":"And during that time, I was working as a labor and"},{"t":255.3,"txt":"delivery nurse, and I was making over"},{"t":258.1,"txt":"$200,000. So I really felt like it was ridiculous that"},{"t":261.9,"txt":"I didn't have any savings."},{"t":263.5,"txt":"I did not really have any investments."},{"t":265.7,"txt":"It definitely felt like I was living paycheck to"},{"t":268.3,"txt":"paycheck. And honestly, I did not have an idea"},{"t":271.8,"txt":"before I started on this journey where my money was"},{"t":274.7,"txt":"going. I wasn't tracking my expenses."},{"t":278,"txt":"In 2015, I set out on a mission to take the"},{"t":282.9,"txt":"same level of intentionality that I had in getting all my"},{"t":286.8,"txt":"other degrees into learning how to better manage my"},{"t":290.6,"txt":"money and fix the money mistakes that had gotten me"},{"t":293.4,"txt":"to that point where I was borrowing money to put"},{"t":296,"txt":"blinds on my windows."},{"t":297.9,"txt":"My total debt at that time, with my mortgage included,"},{"t":302,"txt":"was around $1 million of debt."},{"t":320.6,"txt":"So the first thing that I had to change was to figure"},{"t":324.1,"txt":"out actually how to budget."},{"t":326,"txt":"And I used a method called zero-based budgeting."},{"t":328.9,"txt":"When I mastered that, I was able to,"},{"t":332,"txt":"without working extra, consistently,"},{"t":334.6,"txt":"put about $4,000 a month towards debt."},{"t":338.2,"txt":"It was just those little things that we do daily,"},{"t":341.4,"txt":"unconsciously in our spending that just added up."},{"t":345.6,"txt":"When I was able to figure out my budget,"},{"t":348.6,"txt":"I realized that, number one,"},{"t":350.8,"txt":"I did not have to change anything in my lifestyle,"},{"t":353.5,"txt":"but I was now being intentional so that the"},{"t":356.3,"txt":"things that I was actually spending money on actually"},{"t":359.3,"txt":"felt like something, and they were actually the"},{"t":362.2,"txt":"things that I wanted and desired."},{"t":364.7,"txt":"So as part of my debt payoff plan,"},{"t":367.4,"txt":"I used a strategy called the debt snowball,"},{"t":370.4,"txt":"which is where you line up your debts from your"},{"t":373.4,"txt":"smallest debt to your largest debt based off of"},{"t":376.5,"txt":"the amount of the debt, not the interest rate,"},{"t":378.6,"txt":"the amount of the debt."},{"t":380,"txt":"And you tackle the smallest debt while just paying the"},{"t":383.7,"txt":"minimum on the other debt."},{"t":386,"txt":"Once that smaller debt is paid off,"},{"t":387.8,"txt":"now you have that minimum payment plus whatever extra"},{"t":390.9,"txt":"you're able to put on to that next debt."},{"t":407.1,"txt":"It grew into a business because from there,"},{"t":410.9,"txt":"people asked me to share or brands wanted me to"},{"t":414.6,"txt":"represent them in their businesses."},{"t":417.4,"txt":"And so it became an unintentional business."},{"t":422.1,"txt":"I'm a firm believer that the biggest investment you can"},{"t":425.1,"txt":"make is in yourself."},{"t":426.7,"txt":"And for me, this business is one of the"},{"t":431.6,"txt":"best things that has happened to me."},{"t":433.2,"txt":"It's almost a no brainer to be able to put money into"},{"t":437.7,"txt":"it."},{"t":442.8,"txt":"I believe my business could totally be my full time"},{"t":446.5,"txt":"income source."},{"t":447.8,"txt":"I definitely believe in the next year it can totally"},{"t":451.5,"txt":"replace and far surpass my nursing income."},{"t":455.6,"txt":"The thought of quitting nursing is so hard for me"},{"t":459.6,"txt":"because I love being a nurse."},{"t":461.9,"txt":"But there's also times where,"},{"t":463.8,"txt":"you know, we do experience those lows."},{"t":466.4,"txt":"I think my goal ultimately is not to leave nursing,"},{"t":471.3,"txt":"but to have the flexibility to take those three months"},{"t":474.4,"txt":"off to just work four days a week or something like that."},{"t":478.4,"txt":"I really feel like it's within 1 or 2 years where"},{"t":483.3,"txt":"I can pull back from nursing."},{"t":485.8,"txt":"The goal is going to be to have as much financial"},{"t":488.8,"txt":"independence as possible, not to just retire from work"},{"t":493.5,"txt":"and live on a beach. It's really about getting to do"},{"t":496.3,"txt":"the things that I want to do,"},{"t":498.9,"txt":"and having the opportunity to spend time on the things"},{"t":502.4,"txt":"that are important to me, which right now is my"},{"t":506,"txt":"family."}],"words":[{"t":2.36,"w":"Budgeting"},{"t":2.36,"w":"was,"},{"t":2.36,"w":"I"},{"t":2.36,"w":"felt"},{"t":2.36,"w":"like"},{"t":2.36,"w":"one"},{"t":2.36,"w":"of"},{"t":2.36,"w":"my"},{"t":5.04,"w":"greatest"},{"t":5.04,"w":"superpowers."},{"t":7,"w":"And"},{"t":7,"w":"the"},{"t":7,"w":"word"},{"t":7,"w":"budget"},{"t":7,"w":"to"},{"t":7,"w":"a"},{"t":7,"w":"lot"},{"t":7,"w":"of"},{"t":7,"w":"people"},{"t":7,"w":"instills,"},{"t":10.24,"w":"like"},{"t":10.24,"w":"this"},{"t":10.24,"w":"kind"},{"t":10.24,"w":"of"},{"t":10.24,"w":"fear"},{"t":10.24,"w":"that"},{"t":10.24,"w":"you"},{"t":10.24,"w":"have"},{"t":10.24,"w":"to"},{"t":10.24,"w":"live"},{"t":10.24,"w":"in"},{"t":12.28,"w":"deprivation."},{"t":12.28,"w":"But"},{"t":12.28,"w":"what"},{"t":12.28,"w":"my"},{"t":12.28,"w":"budget"},{"t":12.28,"w":"did"},{"t":12.28,"w":"for"},{"t":12.28,"w":"me"},{"t":12.28,"w":"was"},{"t":12.28,"w":"give"},{"t":16.6,"w":"me"},{"t":16.6,"w":"the"},{"t":16.6,"w":"opportunity"},{"t":16.6,"w":"to"},{"t":16.6,"w":"spend"},{"t":16.6,"w":"money"},{"t":16.6,"w":"on"},{"t":16.6,"w":"the"},{"t":16.6,"w":"things"},{"t":16.6,"w":"that"},{"t":19.68,"w":"were"},{"t":19.68,"w":"super"},{"t":19.68,"w":"important"},{"t":19.68,"w":"to"},{"t